  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Massachusetts had $97M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.5% year over year. The FY2027 to date total covers 3,319 awards and the average award size was $29.2K. State obligations in prior full fiscal years were much larger: FY22 was $17.9B, FY23 was $18.3B, FY24 was $17.8B, FY25 was $19.3B, and FY26 was $19.5B. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest share of FY2027 to date obligations at $67.7M, followed by the Department of the Treasury at $20.4M and the Department of Transportation at $4.3M. CRANE & CO., INC. was the top vendor with $20.4M, and Paper Mills was the largest industry by obligation at $19.2M. The FY2027 to date picture shows concentration in a few agencies, vendors, and industries after a steep year over year decline in obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are FY2027 to date obligations in Massachusetts?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $67.7M, the Department of the Treasury obligated $20.4M, and the Department of Transportation obligated $4.3M. CRANE & CO., INC. received $20.4M and the top three vendors together received a large share of the $97M total. Paper Mills received $19.2M and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing received $12.6M, showing industry concentration in a few NAICS categories."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with recent full fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations were $97M, compared with FY26 obligations of $19.5B and FY25 obligations of $19.3B. Obligations fell 99.5% year over year. The FY2027 to date total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure rather than a full-year total."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Massachusetts?",
      "a": "Massachusetts had $97M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 3,319 awards and the average award size was $29.2K. Prior full fiscal years were much larger: FY22 was $17.9B, FY23 was $18.3B, FY24 was $17.8B, FY25 was $19.3B, and FY26 was $19.5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Massachusetts?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs awarded the most contracts in Massachusetts with $67.7M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Treasury awarded $20.4M and the Department of Transportation awarded $4.3M. Other notable buyers included the Environmental Protection Agency with $2.4M and NASA with $1.7M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Massachusetts?",
      "a": "CRANE & CO., INC. was the largest federal contractor in Massachusetts with $20.4M in FY2027 to date. FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. received $10.9M and PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC received $10.6M. Additional top vendors included DIRECT ENERGY BUSINESS LLC with $9.1M and ABBOTT LABORATORIES INC. with $6.7M."
